<div class="digression" id="thinking"><div><div class="eyebrow">NOT EVERYTHING FITS ON A RÉSUMÉ</div><h2>And then there are the other questions.</h2><p>Experiments in participation, storytelling, systems, and how people respond when rules shift. Several are now included above—not as résumé padding, but as questions worth following.</p><a class="textlink" href="#fragments">Explore the unfinished work ↗</a></div><div><div class="quote">What happens when the audience isn't just watching the story, but helping make it happen?</div><div class="reveal"><strong>A tiny thought experiment</strong><p>Would you rather understand all the rules of an experience before entering it—or discover them as you go?</p><details><summary>Why ask?</summary><div class="reveal-answer" id="revealAnswer">Because the answer changes the experience itself. The disclosure of rules is part of the design. It's also a question worth asking about ordinary systems, not just games.</div></details></div></div></div>